# Awwwards Reference Analysis
Link=https://www.awwwards.com/websites/ui-design/
You are analyzing high-quality web design references.

The reference is inspiration and evidence, NOT a template to copy.

## Analyze

### 1. Layout
- page structure
- container widths
- grid
- columns
- alignment
- whitespace
- section rhythm
- hero composition
- asymmetry

### 2. Typography
- font categories
- display typography
- body typography
- hierarchy
- font sizes
- line heights
- letter spacing
- text widths

### 3. Color
- background colors
- text colors
- accents
- borders
- contrast
- visual hierarchy

### 4. Imagery
- image ratios
- cropping
- image positioning
- full bleed vs contained
- image/text relationships

### 5. Components
- navigation
- buttons
- cards
- forms
- product components
- sections
- footers

### 6. Interaction
- hover behavior
- focus states
- menus
- transitions
- cursor behavior
- scroll behavior

### 7. Motion
Identify:
- entrance animations
- image reveals
- text reveals
- stagger
- scale
- opacity
- transforms
- page transitions
- duration
- easing

Do not recommend motion merely because it looks impressive.

### 8. Responsive behavior

Analyze:
- desktop
- laptop
- tablet
- mobile

Identify what changes between breakpoints.

### 9. UX

Evaluate:
- information hierarchy
- navigation clarity
- CTA hierarchy
- readability
- discoverability
- interaction cost
- accessibility

### 10. Performance

Identify potentially expensive:
- video
- WebGL
- large images
- fonts
- JavaScript
- animation

## Output

Create:

.design/references/<name>/analysis.md

and:

.design/references/<name>/design-dna.md

The Design DNA should summarize the underlying visual principles rather than reproducing exact implementation details.

## Important

Never blindly clone:
- logos
- brand identity
- proprietary artwork
- copy
- distinctive illustrations
- unique assets

Extract principles and create an original implementation.
